1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,328
My watch showed midnight, but the street was frozen mid-stride, locked in a breathless, terrifying silence.

2
00:00:08,628 --> 00:00:15,468
I did this. I bought this extra second using a kiosk that trades my happy memories for time.

3
00:00:15,768 --> 00:00:22,848
Ten seconds cost my first kiss. A minute cost my graduation day. It felt like a fair trade.

4
00:00:23,148 --> 00:00:31,476
The world around me unfroze, people rushing past me unaware that I had stolen a slice of their universe.

5
00:00:31,776 --> 00:00:39,096
Then the chest pain hit, sharp and relentless. My heart demanded payment for the stolen seconds I abused.

6
00:00:39,396 --> 00:00:46,164
I ran back to the alley kiosk, desperate to buy another minute before my heart gave out completely.

7
00:00:46,464 --> 00:00:53,592
The screen flashed red. Account empty. No more happy memories left to trade for your life.

8
00:00:53,892 --> 00:01:02,052
My mind flooded with emptiness. Not just sadness, but a hollow void where my entire life should be.

9
00:01:02,352 --> 00:01:06,960
I had bought so much time that I forgot what I was trying to stay alive for.

10
00:01:07,260 --> 00:01:11,436
Would you trade your happiest day for one more minute of breathing?
